# SEO page rules

## Research first (before any new or reworked page)

1. One primary query; check autocomplete / PAA / SERP top 5 format.
2. Name intent (do / know / compare / navigate) and match page type.
3. Check `docs/KEYWORD-MAP.md` for cannibalization; extend an existing URL when intent overlaps.
4. List 3–6 secondary questions → H2s and FAQ.
5. Follow the full checklist in `docs/PAGE-CHECKLIST.md` (synced from the shared per-page checklist).

## On-page structure

- Title 25–65 chars (aim ~30–60), primary keyword near the start; meta description 70–160 (aim ~120–160); og/twitter match.
- Exactly one H1; logical H2/H3 (no skipped levels).
- Answer first: opening 40–60 words answer the query with a **number or clear verdict** in sentence 1 where one exists.
- Tools: calculator inputs ≤60 words after H1 and above the fold on mobile (390×844); cookie bar ≤56px.
- Hubs: 1–2 sentence numeric lead, then **card grid immediately** (first card above the fold).
- Guides: answer block immediately after H1; byline/dates after the answer.
- Cite primary sources; visible Published / Last updated matching schema.
- Self-referencing canonical from `siteConfig.siteUrl`; trailing slash; no hardcoded site host.
- Schema: BreadcrumbList; WebApplication (tools); Article + FAQPage when FAQ is visible; CollectionPage on hubs/indexes.
- Tool pages link ≥1 topical guide high on the page; no thin query-variant duplicates.
